{"pull": {"id": "number:19045", "number": 19045, "title": "KAFKA-18734: Implemented share partition metrics (KIP-1103)", "state": "closed", "draft": false, "created_at": "2025-02-26T23:12:45Z", "closed_at": "2025-02-28T14:22:27Z", "merged_at": "2025-02-28T14:22:27Z", "user": {"login": "apoorvmittal10", "id": 2861565, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjI4NjE1NjU=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2861565?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10", "html_url": "https://github.com/apoorvmittal10", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/apoorvmittal10/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "The PR implements the SharePartitionMetrics as defined in KIP-1103, with one change. The metric `FetchLockRatio` is defined as `Meter` in KIP but is implemented as `HIstogram`. There was a discussion about same on KIP-1103 discussion where we thought that `FetchLockRatio` is pre-aggregated but while implemeting the rate from `Meter` can go above 100 as `Meter` defines rate per time period. Hence it makes more sense to implement metric `FetchLockRatio` as `Histogram`.", "labels": [{"id": 838330122, "node_id": "MDU6TGFiZWw4MzgzMzAxMjI=", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/kafka/labels/core", "name": "core", "color": "ed5a86", "default": false, "description":